Package: RAssistant
Title: A Lightweight AI Assistant for RStudio
Version: 0.16.1
Authors@R: person("MySimpleSmart", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "120612480+MySimpleSmart@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Opens the existing Source-aware chat assistant in the RStudio
    Viewer. Supports image uploads, optional live console context, contextual R help,
    a project Knowledge Base (PDFs, notes, R examples and custom instructions),
    reviewed Source edits and explicitly approved script validation. Stores optional credentials
    in the operating system credential store, separately from package updates.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    askpass,
    callr,
    commonmark,
    ellmer (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    httpuv,
    jsonlite,
    keyring (>= 1.3.0),
    knitr,
    later,
    remotes,
    rlang,
    rstudioapi,
    shiny (>= 1.14.0)
Suggests:
    httr2,
    pdftools
URL: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant
BugReports: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant/issues
Config/RAssistant/Changes: Put Check updates and Help on separate full-width menu rows, keeping existing button styles.
    Open Chat history on a separate page like Code edit history, with a read-only preview, Rename, Delete, Open chat and Back to chat. Preserve the current conversation and draft while browsing.
    Use Knowledge Base documents only when selected for this chat. Clearing the last selection stops retrieval and new source labels; saved instructions and historical source receipts remain available.
